    1	# Slot 1 — Thread 8 (P2): Batched π_h(x) Baseline
    2	
    3	**Mode:** commit, Thread 8 / OPEN_POSITIVE_TARGETS §P2, slot 1 of (≤4).
    4	**Script:** `slot1_baseline.py` (single-file, parameterised by anchors and H).
    5	**Self-grade target for the slot:** B (empirical baseline + structural
    6	classification of which positive-direction subclaims survive into slot 2).
    7	
    8	## Setup
    9	
    10	For fixed x and h ∈ {2, 4, ..., H} compute:
    11	
    12	```
    13	π_h(x) := #{ p prime, p ≤ x : p + h prime }
    14	```
    15	
    16	Three estimators:
    17	
    18	- **M1 — BATCHED SIEVE.** Sieve `[1, x+H]` once, then for each prime p ≤ x
    19	  test all H/2 candidates p+h. Cost
    20	  `O((x+H) log log x) + O(π(x) · H/2)`.
    21	- **M2 — PER-h SIEVE.** For each h, independent sieve of `[1, x+h]`.
    22	  Cost `M · O((x+h) log log x)`. Measured via single-h timing × M.
    23	- **M3 — HARDY-LITTLEWOOD APPROXIMATION.**
    24	  `HL_h(x) = S_h · li_2(x)` where
    25	  `S_h = 2 C_2 Π_{p|h, p odd} (p−1)/(p−2)`,
    26	  `li_2(x) = ∫_2^x dt / log² t`,
    27	  `C_2 = 0.660161...` (twin-prime constant).
    28	  Per-h cost: trial-divide h — `O(polylog x)` since H = polylog(x) and
    29	  prime factors p ≤ √H.
