n at any tested k; (c) sharpened empirical floor for the closure. Cites E2.14 (refined inline), E2.13 (S87 / S237 — additive-combinatorics analogue confirming HL), E1.10 (chi_P locally indistinguishable from random); composition only, no new edge. Cross-domain ingredient: NONE (same Anderson-localisation transfer-matrix machinery as S88, extended setup parameters only). **Verdict**: C-grade — closure stands, no missed angle, but the closure now has empirical depth via W = primorial(7) (= 510510) that wasn't there before. See `experiments/dynamical/anderson_localisation_chi_p/wtrick_extended_probe_results.md`, `archive/sessions/session416_reverify_e2_14.md`. | 416 |
    883	| §P.P2 batched π_h(x) on h, slot 1 — does the parallel-h Eratosthenes sieve produce per-h amortised polylog cost as M = #h grows, or does it bottom out at Θ(x/log x) (P1-shape)? | EXPERIMENT (B-NEGATIVE on EXACT regime; B-POSITIVE on APPROXIMATE regime — Thread-7-shape transposed to h-axis) | E (E1.5 + S224 + S231 + S240..S244 — per-h amortised cost = Θ(x/log x) for batched-sieve; HL polylog-per-h with √x error matches Hardy-Littlewood prediction) | Thread 8 commit step 1/4 (S418). Built `experiments/analytic/batched_pi_h/slot1_baseline.py` (~280 lines) implementing three estimators of π_h(x) := #{p prime, p ≤ x : p+h prime} for h ∈ {2, 4, ..., H}: M1 BATCHED SIEVE (sieve [1, x+H] once, for each prime p ≤ x test all H/2 candidates p+h), M2 PER-h SIEVE (single-h timing × M for prediction), M3 HARDY-LITTLEWOOD APPROX (HL_h(x) = S_h · li_2(x), S_h = 2 C_2 Π_{p|h, p odd} (p−1)/(p−2), li_2 via scipy.integrate.quad). **Three-anchor table** at x = 10⁵ / 10⁶ / 10⁷ with H = ⌊log²x⌋ even-rounded capped at 200, M = 66 / 95 / 100: T_batched = 0.041 / 0.438 / 3.893 s ⇒ per-h amort = 0.62 / 4.61 / 38.9 ms. M1/M2 batched-vs-per-h speedup at x = 10⁵, 10⁶: 6.71×, 8.85× — **bounded constant, not growing with M**. Per-h amort ratio across decades: 7.7×, 8.5× ≈ π(x) ratios 8.18×, 8.47× — **per-h amortised cost is Θ(π(x)) = Θ(x/log x), NOT polylog**. **H-sweep at x = 10⁶** with H ∈ {20, 50, 100, 200, 400}, M ∈ {10, 25, 50, 100, 200}: per-h amortised = 8.7 → 6.0 → 5.0 → 4.5 → 4.3 ms — clear floor at ~4 ms (set by per-prime per-h test cost: π(10⁶) · 50 ns ≈ 4 ms). **Per-h cost is M-INDEPENDENT for M ≥ 50.** **HL approximation per-h cost** = 0.62 / 1.23 / 0.68 µs — five orders of magnitude faster than batched-sieve, flat in x and M (polylog shape). **HL approximation accuracy**: mean |π_h − HL_h|/√x ≤ 0.10, max ≤ 0.25 across all 261 (x, H, h) cells; matches Hardy-Littlewood's O(√x) conjectural bound. **Structural dichotomy** (the slot's main result): EXACT regime per-h cost = Θ(x/