    884	| §F6 / §P7 — does the dyadic family π(2^k), k = 1..N, admit per-query polylog amortisation beyond generic-magnitude HKM? (NOVELTY_CHALLENGES F6 / OPEN_POSITIVE_TARGETS P7 per-query side) | EXPERIMENT (B-NEGATIVE: three independent structural tests on (π(2^k))_{k=1..56} all return random-baseline values within Monte Carlo noise) | E (E1.1 + E1.5; refines E1.1 inline) | S246 novelty mode. Built `experiments/wildcard/dyadic_pi_structure/dyadic_pi_structure.py`: (1) hard-coded OEIS A007053 reference values π(2^k) for k=0..56, verified k≤18 against sympy.primepi (18/18 exact); (2) computed Li(2^k) and Riemann R(2^k) at 80-decimal mpmath precision, residual r_R(k) = π(2^k) − R(2^k), normalised c_R(k) = r_R(k)/2^{k/2}; (3) Monte Carlo random-binary BM linear-complexity null at length 56 with matched n_pos=25 / n_neg=31 split (4000 shuffles): mean=28.25, std=1.01, p05=27, p95=30; data BM(sign(r_R))=28, sits at 0.25σ below MC mean — F1 (BM ≤ MC p05) FAILS; (4) MC iid-Gaussian lag-1 |autocorr| null (4000 trials): p95=0.250, p99=0.328, p999=0.437; data max |ac| over lags 1..10 = 0.283 at lag 1, below MC p99, Bonferroni-corrected over 10 lags p ≈ 0.4 — F2 (max |ac| ≥ MC p999) FAILS; (5) HKM cost test via fresh subprocess sympy.primepi with no sieve-cache reuse: median T(2^k) / mean(T(2^k − 1), T(2^k + 1)) = 0.998 / 1.047 / 0.995 at k = 28, 30, 32 (avg 1.013) — F3 (dyadic speedup ratio ≤ 0.5) FAILS. **All three F-claims FAIL → B-NEGATIVE per-query closure.** Note: an earlier v1 result with Li-baseline gave spurious lag-1 = 0.87 driven by the smooth -Li(√x)/2 Möbius-series correction; switching to R-baseline (which absorbs the smooth Σ μ(n)/n Li(x^{1/n}) series) eliminates the confound. **Structural reason** (two independent mechanisms): (a) information-theoretic — the explicit-formula zero-sum −Σ_ρ R(x^ρ) ≈ −2√x Σ_n cos(γ_n log x − arg(ρ_n))/|ρ_n| has phases γ_n · k log 2 mod 2π Weyl-equidistributed in k for every γ_n with γ_n irrational, independently of the dyadic for